Kubernetes Architecture
=========================

Kubernetes Architecture simply explaining in my own words is Operator(who will works on kubernetes cluster)

In Kubernetes if we give any command perform any action in k8's how it will works is 
first the request will goes to Control plane(means) in control plane it has 4 components are 1. API(Application Programming Interface) 
                                                                                             2. Control Manager
                                                                                             3. Scheduler
                                                                                             4. etcd

For example as a user(operator) i am giving request as to create a Pod that request will goes to API and requested Pod will get created in worker node in here 
where Pod should get create ? is worker node 1 or NOde 2 ? that will get decide do is SCHEDULER(It will gonna decide on which worker node Pod should get create)
API passed the request to Scheduler here SCHEDULER will decide on which worker nodes pod should get create 
here question is on which parametes it is going to decide how ? 
For example having 4 pods in one worker node and having 2 pods in another worker node now SCHEDULER will get decide to create pods on which worker node pods need 
to be get created finally it will get created in where having less Pods why because pods are less in another worker node so 
now lets talk about free resiurces for example one worker node having 2 cpus free & 4 gb of ram is free and another worker node is having 1 cpu and 2 gb of ram is free 
now SCHEDULER will decide to create a pod on which worker node need to be get created  
how SCHEDULER will know how many pods are exist in a particular worker nodes it will know component called kubelet. 
kubelet work is to monitor the pods continously and pass the information to SCHEDULER through API server like that way SCHEDULER will know how many pods are exist 
in a particular nodes
next component is etcd. etcd its an entire database for your cluster completely Complete information of the cluster will store on etcd and its stores on key value
stores format like yaml format 
4.th component is Controller Manager it means it has 3 types of controler managers 1. Replication Controller 2. Node controller 3. Service controller
In Replication controler in the sence means if we created a pod in a random worker node now what this RC will do is it will keep an eye of created pods in a worker 
node for every 5 seconds like pods are running or not for example in a worker node had 2 pods 1 is working fine and another pod went inactive at this moment
this RC will do watched for this inactive pod it will wait for 30 seconds, after 30 seconds also it is still in inactive means it will went to down state, after that
it will create a new pod for this inactive pod place what is happening here is RC will automatically creates a new pod that means here we can called it as self-healing 

2.Node controller is also same for every 5 seconds it will do monitor and check every servers status in a cluster it is running or not for suppose if we didn't get 
any responses from any servers means Node controller will wait upto 30 seconds, after 30 seconds will Node Controller will get create automatically a new node(server) 
in a cluster 
3. Service Controller is to expose a pods and access the application we will use services in kubernetes Service controller is also same for suppose any service got 
deleted means after 30 seconds it will get created automatically to access the application successfully and to expose a pods successfully. 

Finally overall review on above topic is 1. Replication Controller(RC) -----> PODS will get create automaticcally for this we are using Replication Controller(RC)
                                         2. Node Controller ----------------> Nodes will get create automaticcally for this we are using Node Controller
                                         3. Service Controller -------------> Services will get create automaticcally for this we are using Service Controller

lets talk about Kubernetes Nodes kubelet means it will collect information  from a particular node how many pods are exist in it etc all information 
Now kube-proxy it will maintain the network configurations of the cluster to maintain network policies we will use kube-proxy 



